{
  "$comment": "EXP-1291 Threads v2: the THREAD screen ×4 (a thread IS a root session). Header = the title + ONE tab strip: Conversation · one issue chip per linked issue (session_issues of the ROOT by sortOrder; unsynced issues drop out) · '+' (link/file an issue) · Guide (a dot while the root's guide holds any text or picture); nothing else (no captions, no Stop, no right sidebar). Phones use the strip as the pager. Conversation rows = the root's own session card first (session-card.json, ordinal 1), then the ROOT's messages oldest first (createdAt, ties by id): a card-less row = a message bubble (author user|agent|system, empty bodies skipped; a person's row reads `queued` until the device consumed it); card `session`/`thread_started` = that session's card (ordinal = its place in the tree's creation order; an unsynced target drops out); `question` (question, options, answer, answered = answeredAt set) and `plan` (plan, decision) answer IN the card; `subagent` (title, status); `picture` (attachmentId, width, height, caption; no attachmentId = dropped); `event` = one muted line from `copy.events` ({issue} = the issue's identifier, {pr} = '#<number>'; an unresolvable target or unknown event = dropped); unknown card kinds are dropped. Children's own messages never inline: they show when that session is opened. The composer below = THE session composer box (Composer primitive), placeholder `copy.placeholder`, sending `sessions.send({sessionId: root})` (an ended thread continues server-side in a new child). title = threadTitle: the stored title, else the action name, else the first issue's title, else the first line of the root's first person message (image lines skipped, capped at `titleMax` chars with '…'), else `copy.untitled`; titleDerived = not stored. private = !root.shared (a lock glyph beside the title). live/busy/needsYou aggregate the tree's non-ended sessions. Model = pure `buildSessionThread(input)` (packages/domain-contract/src/session-tree.ts), every mirror replays `cases` comparing the WHOLE expected object. EXP-1306 (owner 2026-10-14): the GUIDE tab ×4 = the root's Guide text over ONE pull request, `guidePullRequest(pullRequests)` (the root's pull_requests; every mirror replays `guidePullRequestCases`): the newest OPEN one (createdAt, ties by the higher number), else the newest MERGED one, else none (a closed PR never counts). When that PR sits in a linear open stack (pr-stack-view.json `stackView` over the repository's pull requests: head = branch, base = prBaseBranch) a `copy.stack` band (the pr-stack glyph, no count) + THE StackRail (top first, the PR's row = the current wash, down to its base branch; a row opens that PR's thread, the hovered/long-pressed row offers Merge through here) leads the Guide; no stack = no block. NO pull-request rows, no inline Merge, no Pull requests band. While the PR is open THE white bottom Merge capsule closes the tab (`testIds.guideMerge`; `Merge stack` on an open-stack member, the one stack confirm). The SESSION view (a session card opens it): while a question or plan card waits on the viewer the CARD takes the composer's place (EXP-820) ×4, the composer leaves and its draft comes back with it: `composerYieldsToCard({live, pendingAsk})` = live AND an unanswered question/plan the viewer may answer; every mirror replays `composerCases`. EXP-1307 (2026-10-14): Open on GitHub + Close PR live in ONE `…` (ui-more) in the thread HEADER's trailing slot ×4 (web/desktop: the title row's end; phones: the header's action slot), shown only while the Guide tab is showing and the Guide has a PR (`guidePullRequest`); `testIds.guideMenu` = the trigger. Its entries = `guideMenuEntries({state, member})` (state = that PR's state, null = no PR; every mirror replays `guideMenuCases`): `open-github` (contract diffUi.openOnGithub, the ui-github glyph) always, then `close-pr` (close-pr.json menuItem, pr-closed glyph, destructive) while the PR is open and the viewer is a member; Close confirms with close-pr.json's dialog (batchLine when the PR links other issues). Empty = no trigger. The bottom capsule stays Merge alone.",
